  "Name": "Kumar2015-TiO2-SiO2-540",
  "Source": "M. Kumar, N. Kumari, P. K. Rao, V. Karar, S. V. Ramagopal, and A. L. Sharma, \"Multi-layer dielectric thin-film optical filters for beam folding applications,\" Proc. SPIE 9654, 96540F (2015). doi:10.1117/12.2181776 - Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 1 (p. 2): TiO2 65 nm, SiO2 105 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1",
  "Notes": "Five-layer TiO2/SiO2 folding mirror for green light, peak reflectance at 540 nm at 45 deg (Multilayer III)\nSpecification: Peak reflectance at 540 nm at 45 deg incidence (beam folding, green).\nReported: Text: peak reflectance at 540 nm (45 deg); peak 'close to 80 %'. Fig. 1 simulated (green curve, approximate): R ~20 % at 400 nm, minimum ~9 % near 425 nm, ~65 % at 475 nm, broad maximum ~79 % around 540-560 nm, ~65 % at 650 nm, ~43 % at 700 nm. Fig. 3 measured (Multilayer III): minimum ~10 % near 415 nm, maximum ~77-78 % around 530-555 nm, ~40 % at 700 nm.\nNotes: Same assumptions as Kumar2015-TiO2-SiO2-480: HLHLH order assumed, TiO2 n = 2.3 (midpoint of 2.2-2.4), unpolarised, 45 deg in air, incoherent BK7 back side included in the paper's simulation. In Fig. 3 'Multilayer III' is the green filter. Total physical thickness 3x65 + 2x105 = 405 nm (not printed).\nLayers from Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 1 (p. 2): TiO2 65 nm, SiO2 105 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R peak 79.5 % at 557 nm, 45 deg, with the back surface; paper peak near 540 nm, R ~80 %.",
